editions to the Iberian Peninsula and the Balkans expanding Tripoli's influence beyond the Crusader states.  Raymond III's military successes earned him a reputation as a formidable warrior and a respected leader among his peers.  He maintained a strong army and strategically positioned fortresses throughout his kingdom.\n\nHis military campaigns were often motivated by a desire to protect Tripoli's interests and secure its borders. He actively participated in the defense of the Crusader states against Muslim incursions.  His military prowess and strategic thinking were instrumental in maintaining the stability and security of Tripoli.\n\n*Later Life and Death*\n\nRaymond III died in 1199 at the age of 55. He was succeeded by his son Raymond IV Count of Tripoli.  His reign is remembered as a golden age for Tripoli a period of prosperity military strength and cultural flourishing. Raymond III's legacy as a strong and effective ruler continues to be celebrated in Tripoli's history. He is remembered as a defender of the Christian faith and a prominent figure in the Crusader era.  His contributions to Tripoli's development and his military achievements cemented his place in the annals of medieval history.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1434636116027832}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.854299135738984e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0874934121966362}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.029306435957551003}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5966804027557373}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.5979602336883545}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.6220458745956421}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5052332282066345}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -1.148343563079834}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.002159527037292719}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00012742661056108773}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0